'''Sio Bibble''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[philosopher]], the [[Governor of Naboo|governor]] of [[Naboo]] and a member of the [[Naboo Royal Advisory Council|Royal Advisory Council]] during the final [[Standard year|years]] of the [[Galactic Republic]]. He stepped down as governor during the early days of the [[Galactic Empire]], which then replaced the position of Naboo's governor with the new role of [[Moff]].

==Biography==
===Early career===
Sio Bibble was [[Reproduction|born]] on [[Naboo]] prior to the [[Invasion of Naboo]].<ref name="DBSioBibble" /> Bibble was elected as the governor of Naboo.<ref name="ECUC">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> During Queen [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]]'s coronation, he and the [[Naboo Royal Advisory Council]] closed the [[Palace Plaza]] for a parade.<ref name="SWP">''[[Star Wars Propaganda: A History of Persuasive Art in the Galaxy]]''</ref> Despite being initially critical of Amidala, he soon came to respect her.<ref name="ECUC">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref>

===Invasion of Naboo===
[[File:Bibble_Naboo_Council.png|thumb|left|250px|Bibble on the Royal Advisory Council after losing contact with Senator Palpatine.]] 
In [[32 BBY]], [[Senator]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]] contacted the Royal Advisory Council only to lose communication. Bibble was one of the first to suspect there would be an invasion. However, [[Queen]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Amidala]] refused to condone any action that would lead them to war. Later, Bibble's suspicions proved correct when Naboo was invaded by the [[Trade Federation]]. Bibble was arrested along with other people on Naboo at that time. Then, [[Jedi Master]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]] and his [[Padawan]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] came to rescue them. Queen Amidala (really her decoy [[Sabé]]) agreed that she should plea to the Senate. Bibble was on high hopes that Senator Palpatine might help them.<ref name="DBSioBibble" /> However, Bibble decided to stay behind to protect his people. Later, Queen Amidala did free Naboo. Bibble attended Jinn's funeral, who was killed in the battle that liberated Naboo. Then, he attended the [["Liberation Day" Parade|celebration]] of Naboo's victory, where [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Queen Amidala]] handed the [[Globe of Peace]] to Boss [[Rugor Nass]].<ref name="Episode I" />

===The Separatist Crisis===
Bibble continued to serve as governor under Amidala's [[Monarch of Naboo|successor]], Queen [[Réillata]].<ref name="Queen's Shadow">''[[Queen's Shadow]]''</ref> In [[22 BBY]], he attended a Council meeting. They talked about how the [[Separatist Crisis]] might become a war and then redirected the conversation to Senator Amidala, who was in danger of being killed and had to hide on Naboo with a bodyguard, [[Anakin Skywalker]].<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref>

===The Clone Wars===
====Service====
[[File:SioBibble-TCWCEJtB.png|thumb|right|200px|Bibble continued to serve through the Clone Wars.]]
Queen [[Jamillia]] was succeeded by Queen [[Neeyutnee]] by [[21 BBY]], whom Bibble also served.<ref name="Blue Shadow Virus">{{TCW|Blue Shadow Virus (episode)}}</ref>

In [[20 BBY]], he greeted Palpatine upon his return to Naboo and attended the [[Festival of Light]]. That night, [[bounty hunter]]s tried to kidnap Palpatine, but their plans were thwarted by Kenobi (who was disguised as [[Rako Hardeen]] at that time). The next morning, Bibble was put in a protection group along with Queen Neeyutnee and Senator Amidala.<ref name="Crisis on Naboo">{{TCW|Crisis on Naboo}}</ref>

====Mission to Bardotta====
In [[19 BBY]], Bibble went with Senator Amidala to the Galactic Senate when Queen [[Julia]] of [[Bardotta]] contacted the Republic. Palpatine presented the queen the people he chose to go to Bardotta: Senator [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]] of [[Alderaan]] and Senator Amidala of Naboo. However, the queen specifically said she wanted [[Junior Representative]] [[Jar Jar Binks]] of Naboo to go, puzzling everyone.<ref name="The Disappeared 1">{{TCW|The Disappeared, Part I}}</ref>

===Imperial Era===
[[File:Bibblemourning.png|thumb|left|250px|Bibble continued as governor into the Imperial Era.]]
Sio Bibble attended the [[Padmé Amidala's funeral|funeral of Padmé Amidala]] shortly after the [[Proclamation of the New Order|formation]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> Around that time, he chose to retire as governor. However, instead of an election being held, in which former [[Naboo Royal Handmaidens|Royal Handmaiden]] [[Saché]] was heavily favored to win, the Empire replaced the position with that of Imperial [[governor]], and appointed [[Quarsh Panaka]] to the position.<ref name="Queen's Shadow" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|I guess there's a reason Bibble keeps getting elected.|[[Rabé Tonsort|Rabé]]|<ref name="Queen's Peril">''[[Queen's Peril]]''</ref>}}
Sio Bibble was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]]<ref name="SWESioBibble" /> who served as the Governor of Naboo and the head of the planet's Royal Advisory Council. He was 1.79 [[meter]]s (5 [[Foot|feet]], 10 inches) tall<ref name="Join the Battle" /> with [[Color|white]] [[hair]], blue [[eye]]s and light skin.<ref name="Episode I" />

Bibble was a dedicated public servant who served as governor. He did not always agree with Queen Amidala, but he supported her and deferred to her judgement. He admired Amidala's lofty goals but did not always share her optimism. He had influence among her other advisers,<ref name="Queen's Peril" /> and was also a [[Philosopher|philosopher]].<ref name="ECUC" />

Bibble was a brave and defiant man in the face of great danger, as he demonstrated when [[Viceroy]] [[Nute Gunray]] from the Trade Federation invaded [[Theed]]<ref name="Episode I" />, though he was completely opposed to violence.<ref name="ECUC">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> Bibble was also known to speak his mind on several important matters like the Separatist Crisis or Gunray's constant trials in the Supreme Courts of the Galactic Republic for his actions.<ref name="Episode II" />More than anything, Bibble cared to an extent for the safety of Queen Amidala as demonstrated during the Trade Federation's invasion of Theed.<ref name="Episode I" /> He later offered advice to Queens Réillata, Jamillia and Neeyutnee. Each monarch relied on Bibble to offer plain talk rather than useless flattery.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Skills and abilities==
As Naboo's governor, Bibble was a talented leader, highly skilled in diplomacy, governance and negotiations. He alongside Queen Amidala led their people during the Trade Federation invasion.<ref name="Episode I" /> He also was effective at legislative strategies.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Sio_Bibble_concept.jpg|thumb|right|Concept art of Sio Bibble by [[Iain McCaig]].]]
Sio Bibble was played by [[Oliver Ford Davies]] in the [[1999]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']].<ref name="Episode I" /> Davies then reprised the role again in [[2002]]'s [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']]<ref name="Episode II" /> and [[2005]]'s [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']].<ref name="Episode III" />

Concept art for Sio Bibble was developed by [[Iain McCaig]].<ref name="DBSioBibble" /> For Bibble's name, however, it was [[Katie Lucas]], daughter of director [[George Lucas]], the one who came up with the name.<ref name="KLTweet1">{{Twitter|KRLgrrl|statuses/52816495872442368|[[Katie Lucas]]|nobackup=1}}</ref>

During the principal photography of ''Attack of the Clones'' in [[Wikipedia:Italy|Italy]], Davies was unable to attend, as he was shooting another film and was in a play. Nine months after Episode II's principal photography had ended, Davies went to reprise the role for a scene shot on a bluescreen stage, and was then digitally inserted into the scene shot in Italy.<ref name="Episode II DVD commentary">{{Film|II}} DVD commentary</ref>

Davies has described Sio Bibble as "benign" and as having "spent most of his time giving good advice that nobody took any notice of."<ref>{{YouTube|video=OdV9pSE7c0I|text=Oliver Ford Davies Sio Bibble Star Wars Interview|channel=@FlicksAndTheCity|name=Flicks And The City|date=2013-11-22}}</ref>

''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]'' and ''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia, New Edition]]'' state that Bibble was elected as the governor of Naboo during King [[Ars Veruna|Veruna]]'s reign, Amidala's predecessor.<ref name="ECUC" /><ref name="Character Encyclopedia New Edition">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia, New Edition]]''</ref> However, ''[[Queen's Peril]]'' later established that [[Sanandrassa]] was Amidala's predecessor.<ref name="Queen's Peril" /> ''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]'' also states he was appointed under Veruna, though he was not Amidala's immediate predecessor.<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> Updated editions of these books, ''[[Star Wars: Character Encyclopedia, Updated and Expanded Edition]]'' and ''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]'' removed mentions of Veruna. The ''Character Encyclopedia'' still states he was elected during Amidala's predecessor,<ref name="Updated Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars: Character Encyclopedia, Updated and Expanded Edition]]''</ref> who would have been [[Sanandrassa]],<ref name="Queen's Peril" /> but the ''Encyclopedia'' states he was elected multiple terms before Amidala,<ref name="Comprehensive Guide to the Galaxy">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> leaving it unclear whether he was appointed under Sanandrassa, during Veruna's unspecified reign, or someone else.

